{"success": true, "name": "continual-arc-puzzle-solving", "file": "references/session-18868900-demo-budget.md", "content": "# Heterogeneous demos: transfer and stopping audit

This session supplied four sharply different examples: a 28×14 input yielding a singleton color, two large periodic/lattice inputs yielding compact 4×6 and 5×3 grids, and a 22×27 lattice yielding 5×3. Their output shapes and palette encodings differ, while the 27×27 test is a periodic 3/4/9/2/7/1 lattice. The singleton output was not a valid basis for the test shape, and a guessed 6×4 block expansion was rejected. These examples demonstrate that output shape must be inferred independently from palette/marker structure and must replay across relevant demos before submission.

Reusable audit: (1) record input and output dimensions and marker coordinates for every pair; (2) distinguish output-shape rule from color/phase rule; (3) normalize geometry and role colors, then require a single candidate to reproduce complete demos; (4) after rejection, reconsider shape and mapping together rather than making a cosmetic variant; (5) request another demo only if an explicit ambiguity remains and the next pair could distinguish candidate outputs. This session did not establish a validated transformation, so do not treat any proposed test output as a known answer.", "file_type": ".md", "_source_path": "/home/USER/continual-arc-baselines/.workbench/stage1/H-hermes-luna6-low-rnd0/frozen/seen/play/users/u066/system/state/hermes/skills/reasoning/continual-arc-puzzle-solving/references/session-18868900-demo-budget.md"}

