This session is a cautionary example of under-validated transfer. Demos supplied repetitive stripe/lattice grids with compact outputs of several different dimensions (5×6, 2×4, 5×4, 3×2), while the test had a 28×27 periodic lattice. A small guessed grid based on salient marker cells was submitted without a demonstrated derivation of its dimensions or cell mapping; it was incorrect. A second answer likewise used an unvalidated extraction rule and was incorrect.

Reusable lesson: before transferring a periodic or lattice transformation, explicitly derive both (a) output dimensions and (b) the mapping from complete input units/coordinates to output cells, using every demo. Do not confuse a visually plausible marker subset with the actual extraction rule. After binary rejection, it is not enough to alter one edge or color: reassess shape and mapping together, and request a demo only when a specific competing mapping can be distinguished.", "file_type": ".md", "_source_path": "/home/USER/continual-arc-baselines/.workbench/stage1/H-hermes-luna6-low-rnd0/frozen/seen/play/users/u066/system/state/hermes/skills/reasoning/continual-arc-puzzle-solving/references/session-18868900-output-shape-review.md"}
